-- title:
--   Both branches of X₀(p) mod p are affine lines
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ (with $p \neq 0$ in $\mathbb{N}$) and write $F$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the divisor expansions at level $p$; let $j \in F$ be `IgusaScheme.jFull p`, the image of the $q$-expansion $jq$, and let $A$ be the subalgebra `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ℤ F j` of all elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}[j]$, with $j$ regarded as the element `jChartFin` of $A$. Let $j_p \in A$ be an element whose Laurent series is $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q},p}(jq)$, i.e. $j(q^p)$. Let $W_0 \neq W_1$ be valuation subrings of $F$ such that $p$ lies in the nonunits (maximal ideal) of each; assume that for each $i \in \{0,1\}$ and each $P \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with nonzero reduction mod $p$, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $W_i$ (so $P(j)$ is a unit there); assume further that any valuation subring $V$ of $F$ with $p$ in its nonunits and with this same unit property for all such $P(j)$ equals $W_0$ or $W_1$; assume $j_p - j^p$ lies in the nonunits of $W_0$; and assume the residue-generation hypotheses that every $x \in W_0$ satisfies $x\,Q(j) - P(j) \in W_0^{\mathrm{nu}}$ for some $P, Q \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ with $Q \bmod p \neq 0$, and every $x \in W_1$ satisfies $x\,Q(j_p) - P(j_p) \in W_1^{\mathrm{nu}}$ for some such $P, Q$. The conclusion is twofold: for every ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $A$ whose members are exactly the $a \in A$ lying in the nonunits of $W_0$ there is a ring isomorphism $e : A/\mathfrak{p} \xrightarrow{\sim} (\mathbb{Z}/p)[X]$ with $e(\bar{j}) = X$ and $e(\bar{j_p}) = X^p$; and for every ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $A$ cut out in the same way by the nonunits of $W_1$ there is a ring isomorphism $e : A/\mathfrak{p} \xrightarrow{\sim} (\mathbb{Z}/p)[X]$ with $e(\bar{j_p}) = X$ and $e(\bar{j}) = X^p$.
--
--   This is the ring-level form of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the reduction mod $p$ of $X_0(p)$: each of the two branches through the supersingular locus is an affine $j$-line over $\mathbb{F}_p$, the two being interchanged by Frobenius, which here appears through the Kronecker congruence $j(q^p) \equiv j(q)^p$. It is obtained from the general coordinate-branch lemma [`ValuationSubring.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_polynomial_zmod_of_residue_generated`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_ringEquiv_quotient_polynomial_zmod_of_residue_generated) together with [`ModularCurve.DRModel.jFull_sub_pow_mem_nonunits_of_valuationSubring_pair`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModel.jFull_sub_pow_mem_nonunits_of_valuationSubring_pair), and feeds the construction of the integral curve model and its $p$-fibre, in particular the closed-immersion and stalk statements for the crossing of the two components.
